## Hints for Future Agents
The fetch scripts must run under macOS /bin/bash 3.2, which is why lib.sh uses parallel indexed arrays and `${arr[@]:-}` instead of associative arrays. An EXIT trap's function return status becomes the script's exit status, so every helper used as a trap must end on a statement that returns 0 in the no-op case.
upstream's replacement AGENTS.md is a rewrite, not a concatenation: the commit-note template has six differently named sections, "third concrete use" became "a heuristic, not a threshold", and the fence guidance was softened. Adopting it changes agent behaviour in every session, so it is a deliberate decision, not a refresh.

